# Project independence

This repository is an academic MAIC Hacksgiving project. It is independent of Direct Supply. Treat every task as local work, or as a deploy of this project to a cloud the user explicitly chooses in the conversation.

## Where work may go

- The laptop: the repo, Docker Compose, a local kind cluster, local files, and local test runs.
- A cloud the user names for this project, such as an AWS account they choose when they ask to deploy. Use only the account, region, and registry they specify.

## Keep Direct Supply out of this project

Do not send this project, its data, images, state, or secrets to Direct Supply systems. That includes Direct Supply git remotes, container registries, Kubernetes clusters, cloud accounts, `*.directsupply.cloud`, and internal chat or ticket tools.

```text
# Allowed when the user asked for their own AWS account
terraform apply    # deploy/terraform with target = "aws"

# Not allowed
git push origin    # when origin is a Direct Supply org
docker push <direct-supply-registry>/comforce-api
```

If a remote, registry, or account looks like it belongs to Direct Supply, stop and ask which destination they want. Do not infer a company destination from the laptop, VPN, or credential files.
